{:workflow/id :eng-003g-review
 :workflow/version 1

 :meta {:name "eng-003g-review"
        :description "Adversarial review of ENG-003G (ep ingest + durable Lucene search) before promotion to done."
        :phases [{:title "Review" :detail "3 lenses on the ENG-003G commit"}
                 {:title "Verify" :detail "2 skeptic votes per finding, quorum 2"}]}

 :run {:model "kimi-for-coding/k3"
       :dir "/home/err/spaces/epiphany"
       :agent-timeout-ms 900000
       :max-concurrency 3}

 :vars
 {:repo "/home/err/spaces/epiphany"
  :cards
  [{:key "eng-003g"
    :path "/home/err/spaces/epiphany/docs/kanban/stories/eng-003g-wire-ep-ingest-and-durable-lucene-search.md"
    :context "FIX-VERIFICATION PASS. The change under review is commits fd20b30 (original) + 2573e7e (review fixes) on branch triage/2026-07-21-assurance-fixes-launcher. An earlier wave of THIS workflow confirmed two blockers, both now claimed fixed in 2573e7e: (1) byte-vs-char span slicing — section-body-text and section-content-hash now use shape.markdown/slice; (2) repository-metadata-file/read! threw on missing repository.edn — now returns nil, resolve-repository updated. Your primary job: try to BREAK those fixes (reproduce the original scenarios: non-ASCII Markdown through ep ingest -> ep search; fresh-repo services-profile ingest). Secondary: hunt any NEW defects introduced by 2573e7e itself (it also changed Mongo list-field decodes from getList to .get, conditional request_id write/decode, and checkpoint OID decode). Gates already green: clojure -M:unit-test => 695 tests, 1777 assertions, 0 failures; manual verification showed fresh-repo services-profile ingest of non-ASCII Markdown extracts 1 section/0 failures with searchable body, and idempotent re-ingest (0 new revisions, 0 dupes). Deliberate deferrals the reviewer must not re-litigate: (1) :local ingest being one-shot/in-memory is documented on the card; (2) embedding projection checkpointing is out of scope; (3) per-resource index partitioning is out of scope; (4) the 2 integration-suite failures are pre-existing baseline."}]
  :lenses
  [{:key "correctness"
    :prompt "Hunt for real correctness bugs in the ingest/search wiring: logic errors, idempotency leaks (duplicate index docs, duplicate observations), wrong port-fn calling conventions (some domain fns call (f nil arg), others (f path arg) — check each call site), span-slicing char-vs-byte offset bugs, error paths that swallow or misreport failures, resource leaks (Mongo connections, Lucene writers/readers)."}
   {:key "architecture-law"
    :prompt "Audit against the repo constitution (AGENTS.md, ADR-000/001/002/003): four-quadrant namespace law (domain pure/zero-IO, infra no domain policy), Git-canonical vs Lucene-rebuildable data authority, never-silent-fallback profile contract, UNAVAILABLE semantics, no new dependencies. Cite the rule each finding violates. Note: main.clj already carries substantial orchestration per ADR-003's unified executable; flag only NEW violations introduced by this commit, not pre-existing structure."}
   {:key "dod-coverage"
    :prompt "Verify every acceptance criterion on the card against the actual code and tests. For each item, name the exact test or evidence that satisfies it, or flag it unmet. Also check the card's own 'Out of scope' list is honored by the implementation."}]}

 :schemas
 {:findings {:type "object"
             :additionalProperties false
             :properties {:findings {:type "array"
                                     :items {:type "object"
                                             :additionalProperties false
                                             :properties {:title {:type "string"}
                                                          :file {:type "string"}
                                                          :detail {:type "string" :description "What is wrong / unmet, with concrete evidence (line refs, failing scenario)"}
                                                          :severity {:type "string" :enum ["blocker" "should-fix" "nit"]}}
                                             :required ["title" "file" "detail" "severity"]}}
                          :dodVerdict {:type "string" :description "For dod-coverage lens only: per-DoD-item evidence table as text; empty string otherwise"}}
             :required ["findings" "dodVerdict"]}
  :verdict {:type "object"
            :additionalProperties false
            :properties {:refuted {:type "boolean" :description "true if the finding is wrong, already handled, out of scope for the card, or not worth acting on"}
                         :reason {:type "string"}}
            :required ["refuted" "reason"]}}

 :stages
 [{:stage/id :review
   :stage/kind :map-agent
   :stage/phase "Review"
   :stage/items {:cartesian [{:bind :card :from [:vars :cards]}
                             {:bind :lens :from [:vars :lenses]}]}
   :stage/agent "ultra-reviewer"
   :stage/schema :findings
   :stage/label "review:{card/key}:{lens/key}"
   :stage/prompt "You are reviewing a change in the repo ({repo}) against its kanban card.\n\nCard: read {card/path} in full (including comment history — earlier reviews may have already fixed things; do not re-report fixed items).\nRepo rules: read {repo}/AGENTS.md if present.\n{card/context}\n\nYour lens: {lens/prompt}\n\nRead the actual source files (and tests) relevant to your lens. Report ONLY findings that would matter to a maintainer deciding whether to promote this card. Do not report style preferences the repo doesn't legislate. If the dod-coverage lens, also fill dodVerdict with the per-item evidence table."}

  {:stage/id :verify
   :stage/kind :vote-fan-out
   :stage/phase "Verify"
   :stage/over :review
   :stage/finding-path [:findings]
   :stage/agent "ultra-skeptic"
   :stage/schema :verdict
   :stage/votes 2
   :stage/quorum 2
   :stage/label "verify:{finding/title|40}"
   :stage/prompt "A code reviewer claims the following about the repo ({repo}), card {card/path}:\n\nTITLE: {finding/title}\nFILE: {finding/file}\nCLAIM: {finding/detail}\nSEVERITY CLAIMED: {finding/severity}\n\nSkeptic pass #{vote/n}: try to REFUTE this. Read the actual code and card (including comment history — the card may already document this as an accepted tradeoff or fixed item). Refute if: the claim is factually wrong, the behavior is deliberate and documented, it is out of the card's delivered scope, or it is too minor to gate a promotion. Default to refuted=true if uncertain."}

  {:stage/id :return
   :stage/kind :return
   :stage/return {:confirmed :surviving :all :flat}}]}
